# The kitchen's declaration: what it can and cannot do. Valla holds it to this.
# Replace it with ~/.config/valla/kitchen.declaration for your own kitchen.
#   files:   the kinds of file it may write (a suffix like .rs, or an exact name like .gitignore)
#   can:     what it handles
#   cannot:  what it does not handle, will not attempt, or cannot check
#   needs:   what it requires from the house

files: .rs .toml .nix .py .md .txt .html .css .js .json .sh .sql .yaml .yml .csv .tsv .sensors .lexicon .standards .gitignore
can: write and change code in Rust, Python, Nix, shell, HTML, CSS and JavaScript
can: write docs, config files, sensors and tests
cannot: run code or tests; the sensors do that
cannot: touch real hardware, or prove a hardware standard is met; only a sensor on the machine can
cannot: reach the internet or see any file it was not shown
cannot: write binary files (images, databases, archives)
needs: the request, the committed files of the house, and the house standards
needs: sensors in valla.sensors to show the work is done
